 "verdict": {
  "headline": "The ballistic engine (a persistent click-rate difference between the two clones) switches on across the ridge: the fraction of runs with a nonzero click-count difference between clones crosses 1/2 at U_d/s_d = 0.443 [0.420, 0.466], indistinguishable from the measured ridge 0.407 [0.347, 0.450].",
  "supporting": "clone-front click probability p_click rises 0.008 -> 0.20 (ridge) -> 1.0 across the ridge; ensemble gap-variance growth exponent chi_late rises from a frozen plateau ~0.3 through 0.71 at the ridge to ~1.4 (super-diffusive) at U_d/s_d>=1.2, crossing the diffusive value 1 at 0.495 [0.466, 0.639] (one rung above the ridge; intervals adjacent, not overlapping).",
  "refuted_form": "The specific claim 'sigma_DeltaR falls below the diffusive floor' is NOT supported as a curve-crossing statement: the slope-based sigma_DeltaR exceeds any horizon-appropriate diffusive floor at every rung sampled (0.05-10), and below the ridge the fitted slope is a bounded fluctuation whose SD decays with observation window (exponent -0.74 at U_d/s_d=0.05), not an intensive rate. The mechanism should be stated as ratchet ARREST (no persistent Delta R exists) below the ridge, not as a rate spread crossing a floor."
